# Intel Data Streaming Accelerator (DSA) and In-Memory Analytics Accelerator
# (IAA), via the idxd driver.  Per-fleet hardware, like the NICs.
#
# Why a hypervisor fleet cares: DSA does large memory copies and zeroing
# without burning a core, which is the hot path of live migration (copying
# guest pages) and of scrubbing a VM's memory before handing it to the next
# tenant.  IAA does compression, which is what makes migrating a large guest
# over a shared fabric affordable.
#
#   make ACCEL=intel-dsa PROFILE=hypervisor build
CONFIG_DMADEVICES=y
CONFIG_INTEL_IDXD=y
CONFIG_INTEL_IOATDMA=y
# Shared virtual addressing hands the device the CPU page tables.  The rest of
# this config refuses that for the IOMMU; it refuses it here too.  Use
# dedicated work queues with an explicit IOVA mapping instead.
# CONFIG_INTEL_IDXD_SVM is not set
